### Order requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client):
### click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### Place an order (place_order procedure: one transaction)
# @name order
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 24,
  "shippingAddressId": 24,
  "items": [
    { "productId": 456, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 63, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Read it
GET {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}

### Ship it (row lock + trigger logs NEW -> SHIPPED)
POST {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/ship

### Shipping again fails: 409
POST {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/ship

### Status history written by the trigger
GET {{base}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}/status-history

### Place another order and cancel it (cancel_order procedure returns the stock)
# @name second
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 24, "items": [ { "productId": 3, "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
POST {{base}}/orders/{{second.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

###
GET {{base}}/orders/{{second.response.body.$.id}}/status-history

### Out of stock: the whole order is rolled back, 409
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 24, "items": [ { "productId": 3, "quantity": 1 }, { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### The customer's order history (v_order_summary view)
GET {{base}}/customers/24/orders
